    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0833" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg785"/>

                <head>Mr. Van Valkenburgh to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Yokohama,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 3, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    inclosure No. 1, a copy of letter from Higashi Kuze Chinjio, minister for
                    foreign affairs, informing me that from the 1st of September next Osaka will be
                    a port of entry.</p>
                <p>Among the foreign merchants at Hiogo and Osaka, the opinions of the relative
                    future importance of those two places have been much divided, and by this
                    measure they are now placed on a par.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d358-a1.xml" xpointer="d358-a1"/>
            </div>
